# One worktree per chat
Parallel chats share one checkout; a branch switch or commit there hits another ticket (#585, #624, #655).

- Before the first edit: `scripts/ticket-worktree.sh <branch>` (e.g. `fix/731-review-lang`). Edit/test/commit/push only under `.worktrees/`. If it warns an open PR or worktree already covers the ticket/files, read that first (#2969).
- Worktree is locked to this chat (#2244). If another live chat holds it, stop and tell Carlos; `--take` only when he says so. If pre-flight says yours was taken, stop.
- Main checkout: read only—never `switch`/`checkout`/`stash`/`reset`/`commit`/`pull`.
- Before every commit: `git branch --show-current` must be the ticket branch.
- After merge: `git worktree remove .worktrees/<dir>` and `git branch -D <branch>`.
